<template>
    <SiteShell page="roadmap">
        <div class="page-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Roadmap</span>
            <h1>Phases, not promises</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                The toolbox grows only when a phase ships with tests. There are no
                dates here, no version numbers and no claim that an unimplemented
                phase is around the corner.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="phase phase--done">
                <header class="phase__head">
                    <span class="phase__index">01</span>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Triage and byte-level kernel</h2>
                        <p class="phase__sub">Shipped in this build</p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="chip chip--accent">available</span>
                </header>
                <div class="cols-2">
                    <ul>
                        <li>Container detection for PE, ELF, Mach-O and unknown bytes.</li>
                        <li>PE, ELF and Mach-O headers, sections and symbol tables.</li>
                        <li>Import, export and debug facts across PE and ELF.</li>
                        <li>Strings in ASCII and UTF-16LE, hex dumps and entropy.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <ul>
                        <li>RVA, virtual-address and file-offset mapping.</li>
                        <li>x86/x64 disassembly and CPython 3.11–3.13 bytecode.</li>
                        <li>Unpack for 7z, asar, NSIS and PyInstaller, plus inflate.</li>
                        <li>Carve, find, dump, diff and hash-verified patches.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="phase">
                <header class="phase__head">
                    <span class="phase__index">02</span>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Bytecode and script layer</h2>
                        <p class="phase__sub">Planned</p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="chip">planned</span>
                </header>
                <div class="cols-2">
                    <ul>
                        <li>CPython versions beyond 3.11–3.13 in <code>disasm</code>.</li>
                        <li>Code-object filtering that follows calls between modules.</li>
                        <li>Raw marshal streams from wrappers the engine cannot name.</li>
                        <li>Clearer opcode errors when a magic number disagrees.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <ul>
                        <li>PYZ reconstruction across a package tree, not one file.</li>
                        <li>Nested PyInstaller archives that hide further containers.</li>
                        <li>Script formats listed only once a decoder exists.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <p class="phase__note">
                    <code>disasm</code> today covers x86, x64 and CPython 3.11–3.13.
                    Nothing above is wired to a command, and no pseudo-code or type
                    recovery is promised here.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="phase">
                <header class="phase__head">
                    <span class="phase__index">03</span>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Deeper container unpacking</h2>
                        <p class="phase__sub">Not started</p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="chip">planned</span>
                </header>
                <div class="cols-2">
                    <ul>
                        <li>Installer and archive families beyond 7z, asar, NSIS and PyInstaller.</li>
                        <li>Automatic discovery of containers nested inside an unpacked tree.</li>
                        <li>Per-entry extraction limits that stay explicit.</li>
                        <li>Stronger Tauri asset recovery on partial bundles.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Overlay carving driven by entropy instead of markers.</li>
                        <li>Container-level diff between two installers.</li>
                        <li>No silent extraction when a container is only partly understood.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <p class="phase__note">
                    <code>unpack</code> already expands 7z, asar, NSIS and PyInstaller.
                    A new family stays off this page until a decoder exists.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="phase">
                <header class="phase__head">
                    <span class="phase__index">04</span>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Verifiable modification</h2>
                        <p class="phase__sub">Not started</p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="chip">planned</span>
                </header>
                <div class="cols-2">
                    <ul>
                        <li>Section-aware patch previews before any byte is written.</li>
                        <li>Patch plans that can be replayed and diffed as a file.</li>
                        <li>Explicit refusal when a patch crosses a header boundary.</li>
                        <li>Diff-driven patching that names each changed region.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Hash chains that cover every intermediate write.</li>
                        <li>Structured reports that a CI check can read.</li>
                        <li>A debugger and a decompiler stay out of scope.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <p class="phase__note">
                    Patch reports already carry before/after hashes. Reproducible patch
                    plans are not implemented, and nothing here is promised by a menu.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="band">
            <div>
                <span class="eyebrow">How this list changes</span>
                <h2>A phase moves only with tests</h2>
                <p>
                    A capability appears here as available when the command line, the
                    studio and the engine tests all cover it. Until then the capability
                    matrix reports it as unsupported.
                </p>
            </div>
            <Link to="FeaturesPage" class="btn btn--ghost">
                Read the features
            </Link>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-band">
            <div>
                <h2>Follow the work</h2>
